<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26360" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Leucippus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λεύκιππος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The father of Phœbe and Hilaira, who were
				carried off by Castor and Pollux</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 5,
				709</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Leucippis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>a
				daughter of Leucippus</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 2,
				15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">te rapuit Theseus, geminas Leucippidas illi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					H. 16, 327</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 80</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Lact. 1,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A son of Hercules</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				162</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Grecian philosopher, a disciple of Zeno the
				Eleatic</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 37, 118</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id.
				N. D. 1, 24, 66</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
